---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { links } from '../i18n/links';
---

<Page title="Support | EatMatrix" description="Help with the EatMatrix app: subscriptions, scanning, account and data questions.">
  <section class="prose-em mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Support</h1>
    <p>
      Questions about EatMatrix? Email <a href={`mailto:${links.supportEmail}`}>{links.supportEmail}</a> and we’ll get back to you. Include your device
      model and, if it helps, a photo of the label you scanned.
    </p>
    <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
    <p>
      EatMatrix subscriptions are billed through the App Store. To cancel or change a plan: open <strong>Settings → your name → Subscriptions</strong>
      on your iPhone. Cancelling stops the next renewal; you keep access until the current period ends.
    </p>
    <h2>Deleting your account and data</h2>
    <p>
      In the app, open <strong>Account → Delete account</strong>. This removes your profile, saved allergens and preferences, and the scan history on
      your device. Subscriptions are managed separately by Apple (see above).
    </p>
    <h2>Scanning tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Fill the frame with the ingredient list; the app reads the label itself — no barcode needed.</li>
      <li>If the label isn’t readable, point at the front of the pack: EatMatrix recognizes the product and verifies its ingredients online.</li>
      <li>Hold steady for a second — the frame fills when a product is locked.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Page>
